List recent jobs (GET /v1/runners/jobs), newest first.

--repo is owner/name. --status filters by job status. DURATION is start to
finish, or the time so far for a job still running.

When older jobs exist the output ends with a cursor; pass it as --before to
read the next page. With --json the result is {"jobs": [...], "next_cursor":
"..."}, and next_cursor is empty on the last page.

Usage:
  anona-compute runners jobs [flags]

Flags:
      --before string   page cursor: list jobs older than the previous page (printed when more exist)
  -h, --help            help for jobs
      --limit int       how many jobs to list (default 20)
      --repo string     only jobs of this repository (owner/name)
      --status string   only jobs with this status

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, ANONA_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each non-streaming request, 0 = none (create, pause, resume and fork: 3m0s unless set; streams and uploads are never cut off) (default 1m0s)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
